---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of Use | ${SITE.name}`}
  description="The terms on which you may use this site and its calculators."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Terms' }]}
  noAds
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="tool-header">
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="tool-standfirst">Last updated 7 August 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-body">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Using this site</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.name} is free to use. There is no account, no subscription and no paywall. By using
          the site you accept these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Information, not advice</h2>
        <p>
          Everything here is general information about UK tax. It is <strong>not</strong> financial,
          tax, legal or investment advice, and it does not take account of your circumstances. We are
          not regulated by the Financial Conduct Authority and we do not provide regulated advice.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before acting on anything you read here, check it with a qualified accountant, a regulated
          financial adviser, or HMRC. See our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Accuracy</h2>
        <p>
          We take considerable care to be accurate: rates come from primary sources, are dated, and
          the calculation engine is covered by unit tests built from HMRC worked examples.
          <a href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Even so, we cannot guarantee that every figure is correct or current. Tax rules change,
          sometimes mid-year, and no calculator can capture every personal circumstance. Use these
          tools as estimates, not as the final word.
        </p>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising from use of this
          site or reliance on its content. That includes decisions about employment, property
          purchases, incorporation, pensions or tax filings. Nothing here limits liability for death,
          personal injury or fraud caused by our negligence, which cannot lawfully be excluded.
        </p>

        <h2>Content and copyright</h2>
        <p>
          The text, design and code of this site belong to us. You may read it, print it and share
          links freely. You may not republish substantial portions as your own, or copy the
          calculators for a competing site.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tax rates and thresholds are facts published by government and belong to nobody. Quoting
          our figures with a link back is welcome.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to keep the site available but do not guarantee it. We may change, suspend or
          withdraw any part of it without notice.
        </p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>
          We link to gov.uk, Revenue Scotland, the Welsh Revenue Authority and similar sources. We
          are not responsible for their content, and a link is not an endorsement.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and
          Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p><a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
